# Frontend Naming: Incremental Rename Plan

Apply this rule **only** when the current change already edits one of the paths above (or its post-rename equivalent). General `Page*` / `Button*` conventions and component/file naming live in **`react-js-cursor-rule.mdc`**.

## Rename targets (local scope only)

| Current path | Target component file |
|-----|----|
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/Layout.jsx` | `PageLayoutMain.jsx` |
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/App.jsx` | `AppMachine.jsx` (SPA entry; `App.jsx` remains a thin re-export until removed) |
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/pages/JobList.jsx` | `PageJobList.jsx` |
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/pages/JobDetail.jsx` | `PageJobDetail.jsx` |
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/pages/Search.jsx` | `PageSearch.jsx` |

## Guardrails

- Rename **only** when the same PR already modifies that target file (do not open renames-only PRs for these paths).
- Update **all** imports and matching tests in the **same** change.
- Do **not** perform repo-wide naming churn unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Keep behavior unchanged; naming consistency only.

## Overlap

- **`react-js-cursor-rule.mdc`** — Naming Conventions, incremental adoption pointer, and Bokeh/CSP expectations for touched frontend files.
